The wrapper is already a single inlined setter call with constant arguments, so any rewrite would add overhead or risk behavioral change. I kept it identical to preserve the best measured performance (1.000).

```cpp
    void SetHeliumContent(FIT_UINT8 heliumContent)
    {
        SetFieldUINT8Value(0, heliumContent, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```